cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or discuss this certificate extension, please cite this repository version."
title: "Erdős Problem #287: 60-step good-prime-chain certificate extension"
authors:
  - family-names: "Tripodo"
    given-names: "John"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jjtripodo-lgtm/erdos287-certificate-extension"
url: "https://github.com/jjtripodo-lgtm/erdos287-certificate-extension"
abstract: >-
  A replayable 60-step extension of the public good-prime-chain certificate
  framework for Erdős Problem #287. The bundle includes recursive
  Pocklington-style primality certificates, a pure-Python verifier, negative
  controls, exact expected output, and a checksum manifest. It is a finite
  certificate contribution, not a proof of Erdős Problem #287.
keywords:
  - "Erdős Problem #287"
  - "computational number theory"
  - "primality certificate"
  - "good-prime chain"
  - "reproducible mathematics"
